  "english": "7. Tuesday. Tone 4 [DG]. Fathers of Egypt: Paul, etc.\n\n9. Thursday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\n\n12. Sunday. Tone 2 [BK]. Third. Carnival of the Fast of Saint James. Father [Hymn], Tone 2 [bk]: \"Who the servant.\" Dismissal [Hymn, Hambartsi], Tone 2 [bk]: \"They anticipated.\"\n\n19. Sunday. Tone 2 [BCh]. Fourth. Father [Hymn], Tone 3 [gd]: \"Glorified Son.\" Dismissal [Hymn, Hambartsi], Tone 2 [bdz]: \"At the tomb,\" and \"They came to the tomb,\" and \"Voice of good tidings,\" and \"Today they rejoiced.\"\n\n20. Monday. Tone 2 [BK]. Ignatius and Ade [Addei] the Patriarchs, Maruthas, and Theopompus the Bishops, and Theonas, etc.\n\n21. Tuesday. Tone 3 [GDz]. King Abgar.\n\n23. Thursday. Tone 4 [DZ]. David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n\n26. Sunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Fifth. Father [Hymn], Tone 3 [gk]: \"Pre-eternal.\" Dismissal [Hymn, Hambartsi], Tone 1 [ak]: \"Wonderful Resurrection.\"\n\n29. Wednesday. Tone 3 [GDz]. Father [Hymn], Tone 3 [gk]: \"Blessed are you, Lord God of our fathers.\" Carnival of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n30. Thursday. Tone 3 [GK]. Fast of the Nativity. Father [Hymn] of the Fast, Tone 4 [dk]: \"God of our fathers, praised are you forever.\"\n\nJanuary\n\n2. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Sixth [Sunday] of the Fast. Dismissal [Hymn, Hambartsi], Tone 1 [adz]: \"Awful vision,\" to the end.\n\n3. Monday. Tone 1 [AK]. Fast. Father [Hymn] of the Fast, Tone 1 [adz]: \"The youths sang.\"\n\n5. Tuesday. Tone 2 [BK]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ.\n\nSeven-Day Cycle of the Romans.\n\n29. Sunday. Tone 1 [ACh]. Easter. Day of the Resurrection of Christ our God. And see the others in order in the First Volume.\n\n7. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AK]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n\nMay\n\n17. Sunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Coming of the Holy Spirit. Carnival of the Fast of Elijah.\n\n24. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. First. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Father [Hymn], Tone 3 [dz]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe.\"\n\nJuly\n\n5. Sunday. Tone 2 [BZ]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The dispensation of eating meat is five weeks. See in the other volume.\n\nJanuary\n\n6. Tuesday. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The dispensation of eating meat is thirteen days.\n\n15. Thursday. John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n\n17. Saturday. Peter the Patriarch, Blaise the Bishop, and Absalom the Deacon.\n\n18. Sunday. Carnival of the Fast of the Catechumens. Father [Hymn], Tone 4 [dz]: \"Dawn.\"\n\n25. Sunday. Saint Sarkis. Father [Hymn], Tone 4 [dz]: \"Glorifying the name.\"\n\n28. Monday. Atomian Saints, and Theodore the Soldier. And see the others in the First Volume up to Vardavar.\n\nFebruary\n\n8. Sunday. Tone 4 [DK]. True Carnival [Great Lent Carnival].\n\n14. Saturday. Tone 3 [GK]. Presentation of the Lord [Tiarn'ndaraj].",
